A||||8||Master_Sushi||Dogbone help!||||8||
Z||000000||Master_Sushi||11-16-2001||01:55 PM||||Ok, I've been doing so much work on my fiero recently I am going crazy. It seems like I fix one stupid things and I find something else wrong when repairing it.<BR>Anyway, I was out driveing my 84se around last night after replacing the cat with a "test" pipe. I got home and parked it in the driveway. I opened the decklid like I allways do, to make sure everything was in good shape. Then I notice one of the dogbone nuts fell off and the bolts almost all the way out. So I pull the bolt out with vice grips and the engine moves about 2 inchs. NOW I CANT GET THE THING BACK IN! I have tried everything. I even jacked up the car to get all the weight off it and I still cant move the engine enough to line up the bolt holes. I even took out my spare tire jack and tried to move the engine with it. That didnt work at all, so I went nuts and ended up smashing my jack with a big hammer <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. I'm at a loss now and don't know what to do! Are my engine/trans mounts shot or something? What else can I try? Please help me!!! ||||reg||8
Z||000001||watts||11-16-2001||02:02 PM||||Point the car downhill.  Stick it in gear (oh, it IS a standard, right?) and push (a helper here is a bonus).  It'll roll over a bit and you stuff in the bolt.  Done it solo a number of times on mine and others that way.<P>If the engine flips the wrong way, put in reverse then do it again (it's been a bit, and I can't remember if it's 1st or reverse you should use!)<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||11-16-2001||02:16 PM||||I lined up the holes using a crowbar to pry engine aft using both hands and lots of leverage (weight).  My helper managed to insert bolt in dogbone and bracket.  Whew!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||11-16-2001||02:37 PM||||Thats for the quick replies. I tried both of those and it still dosen't want to move enough. It is a stick shift and im using a fierostore ultimate dogbone. I have been working on it more, I noticed a huge amount of play in the engine mount on the trannie. Could this cause the prob? The engine will move towards the firewall, but dosen't want to move at all towards the trunk which is what I need it to do! ahhhhhhhhahahahah  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||11-16-2001||03:04 PM||||Sounds like one or more bad engine/tranny mounts.  Their cheap, so go ahead and replace them, if you're in doubt.  I got tranny mounts for $9 each at Advance Auto.  I hear the engine mounts aren't much more.<P>Or you could get the hand made poly tranny and engine mounts from West Coast Fiero for about $65 each.  Whichever you think is the better setup for your car.||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnF||11-16-2001||03:08 PM||||You can insert a small hydraulic jack horizontally between the firewall and the engine forward side and pump until holes line up.<P>BTW - the mount change is a great suggestion.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Master_Sushi||11-16-2001||04:20 PM||||Yes! I got it fixed   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I stuck a jack between the firewall and the engine to push it back. Wasn't easy and this was probably jsut a temp fix. I will probably replace the trannie/engine mounts later.<P>Thanks for all the quick help!<P>Note to self, don't work on car at 1am after long bad day when in a very bad mood or things get smashed. lol<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 11-16-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000007||JD86GT350||11-16-2001||05:03 PM||||I put in the fiero store ultimate dog bone on my '84 SE as well, I used the lug wrench from under the hood, found a good solid pry point on the engine, and pulled with one hand while I stuck the bolt in with the other.  It sure wasn't easy, but I did manage to get it done solo with a few tries.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fldevel||11-16-2001||05:22 PM||||i think i stuck the car in either reverse or 1st gear and let off on the clutch untill the holes where lined up while my dad put the bolt back in the hole ||||reg||1
